1b:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"'Does that make sense?' reliably produces a yes. It asks the patient to assess their own understanding and to admit a shortfall to a clinician, and most people will not. Teach-back asks them to demonstrate it instead: 'I want to make sure I explained that well — can you tell me how you'll take this?'"}]
1c:["$","p","2",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"The framing matters. Teach-back puts the burden on your explanation rather than their comprehension, which removes the shame that keeps people from admitting confusion. It is not a quiz; it is checking your own work."}]
1d:["$","figure","3",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Instead of"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Say"}],["$","th","2",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Because"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Hypertension"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"High blood pressure"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Plain language reaches more people"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Take PO BID"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Take one by mouth twice a day, morning and evening"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Abbreviations are for records, not patients"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Do you understand?"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Tell me how you'll take this at home"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Demonstration reveals what agreement conceals"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"You need to comply with the regimen"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Let's find a schedule that fits your day"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Collaboration works better than instruction"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"The doctor will discuss your results"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"The doctor will call you Thursday about your results"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Specifics reduce anxiety"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Clear communication"}]]}]
1e:["$","div","4",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"Use a qualified medical interpreter when there is a language barrier — never a family member, and never a child. Family members summarize, soften, and omit, particularly around difficult topics, and using a child as interpreter is both a serious clinical risk and a harm to the child. Patients have a right to interpretation, and practices receiving federal funds have an obligation to provide it. Speak to the patient, not to the interpreter, and use ordinary first-person sentences."]}]
1f:["$","figure","5",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Do"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Why"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Let them finish without interrupting"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Interruption escalates; being heard de-escalates"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Lower your voice and slow down"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"People tend to match the calmer register over time"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Acknowledge the feeling before the facts"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"'You've been waiting a long time and that's frustrating' costs nothing and lands"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Say what you can do, not what you cannot"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"'Let me find out where things stand' beats 'there's nothing I can do'"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Keep an exit path and stay aware of your surroundings"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Almost all anger stays verbal, and your safety still comes first"}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Get help early if it escalates"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Involving a supervisor is standard practice, not a personal failure"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"De-escalating an angry patient"}]]}]
20:["$","$L24","6",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"You have explained a new medication schedule. What is the most reliable way to confirm the patient understands?","options":["Ask 'do you have any questions?'","Ask them to describe in their own words how they will take it at home","Ask 'does that make sense?'","Give written instructions and ask them to read them later"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Teach-back asks the patient to demonstrate understanding rather than assess it. Yes-or-no questions reliably produce a yes, because admitting confusion to a clinician feels like admitting a failing. Framing it as checking your own explanation removes that barrier.","optionRationales":["Patients often have questions they cannot yet formulate, and this still requires them to volunteer a shortfall.","Correct. Demonstration reveals what a yes-or-no question conceals.","This is the question that reliably produces a false yes.","Written instructions are a valuable supplement but do not confirm understanding, and assume literacy in that language."]}}]
